WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:06.989
This giant rope creature perplexed us all as he sort of dabbed us onto the cliff before the Fountainhead Palace.

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.899
While it's mentioned in no item descriptions

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:14.460
We can actually make an educated guess about what he represents

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:19.640
So let's tie a knot in it once and for- I'm so sorry about the pun

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:24.400
A shimenawa or enclosing rope is a length of hemp or rice straw

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:30.740
That's commonly found woven around torii gates, shinto shrines, and also sacred landmarks

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:34.940
They're here to act as a sort of ward against evil spirits

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.700
Or to indicate passage into a pure, sacred space

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:41.580
Quite a few of these exist in game,

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:47.430
For example, there's the gate right before the valley that houses the Sacred Serpent God and

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:53.759
Since the Divine Dragon looks about 20 times as divine as the Serpent God

00:00:53.789 --> 00:00:56.759
I guess they needed a bigger rope for the divine realm

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:01.949
Blocking our way to said realm however, is the real Corrupted Monk

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:05.510
A warrior woman who guards the Vermillion bridge

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:13.910
So one thing that marks female warriors as of the Okami clan is a vulnerability to Sabimaru's poison

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.010
She doesn't have that vulnerability

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:21.139
But what she does have is the signature laugh and movement of the Okami

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:27.050
Which marks her as a part of their clan, but perhaps she is not a part of their bloodline

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:28.260
Anyway

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:34.360
She has some really fascinating additions to her character compared to the rest of the Okami

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.380
First and foremost

00:01:35.660 --> 00:01:37.220
She's infested. Hence

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:38.640
She's immortal and

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:46.040
This happened to be a quality that the Fountainhead thought would be quite appropriate for an eternal watcher of their palace

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.520
Her true name is Priestess Yao

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:55.760
and this is a name that user tsurumaru on reddit thinks is a reference to Yao Bikuni

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:03.760
A fisherman's daughter who became immortal after eating the flesh of a ningyo and I completely agree with this theory

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:11.540
So a ningyo is best translated to mermaid for those of us in the West though more accurately

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:19.940
it's described as a fish creature with shining scales, a humanoid face, and the mouth of a monkey

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:24.420
In the story of Yao Bikuni, she eats the flesh of the ningyo and

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:28.920
Those who do so are said to be blessed with incredible longevity

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:33.829
And this is what happens to Yao Bikuni who in the story

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:37.309
Went on to become a wandering, immortal priestess

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:42.080
So there's clearly a parallel here to Priestess Yao, the Corrupted Monk

00:02:42.209 --> 00:02:48.319
Which leads me to believe that Priestess Yao may have eaten immortal ningyo flesh as well

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:54.660
Because the Divine Dragon, in fact, is called the Ningyo Dragon in the game's hidden files and

00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:02.420
Related to the Divine Dragon through a Chinese legend are the Great Carp. The Great Carp are also a type of ningyo

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:09.460
They're a fish with human origins because the pot nobles all aspire to become a Great Carp

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:15.840
Pot Noble: If you ever happen across another pot like mine ignore any requests he makes of you.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:23.940
Pot Noble: He's the shame of our clan, he's a treasonous villain who attempted to kill the Great Carp for his own benefit

00:03:24.319 --> 00:03:25.130
Thus

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:32.229
There have been many Great Carp over the years and you can find their corpses littering the Fountainhead lake bed

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:37.380
All of these rotting corpses are a sort of testament to the ambition,

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:42.960
the backstabbing, and the desperation of the Pot Nobles to become eternal

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:48.980
Pot Noble: Soon, I will be a carp. And as age withers you away,

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:57.040
Pot Noble: as you sit powerless in the face of eternity, I will be the new Great Carp

00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:02.540
Curiously, one such corpse is infested with luminescent centipede creatures

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:07.239
Which may well explain the infestation of Priestess Yao

00:04:07.239 --> 00:04:12.219
If she did indeed eat the ningyo flesh like her namesake did

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:19.570
So this is a really strong theory to think it could be this Japanese legend about eating the flesh of the ningyo

00:04:19.729 --> 00:04:25.689
which is the missing puzzle piece to us understanding where the infestation comes from and

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:33.600
at the very least it is the Fountainhead rejuvenating waters that spread the infestation throughout all of Ashina

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:38.640
As many of the infested have clearly drank deeply of these waters

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:46.510
Near the infested corpse of the Great Carp is the fallen spirit of Yashariku who haunts the bottom of the lake

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:50.709
so the headless are ruined forms of Ashina's heroes and

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:54.609
Yashariku in particular has a really interesting story

00:04:54.919 --> 00:05:01.359
So he died to the palace Nobles but his spiritfall states that he might not have

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.700
Had his twin been at his side

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:06.910
Alas, his twin was lost in childbirth

00:05:07.039 --> 00:05:12.429
Which goes on to explain why we lose half our health when using his item and

00:05:12.919 --> 00:05:20.369
Why a second apparition fights beside him below the lake. He was never quiet whole even after death

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:24.779
Much of the architecture below the lake has become uninhabitable

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:28.020
Thanks to the overflow of divine water and

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:31.709
There's no one here capable of rebuilding this because

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:40.820
Their civilization is now literally comprised of a warrior caste in the Okami, and a noble caste with the palace Nobles

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:46.700
And even more of their area is in the process of being destroyed by the Great Carp

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:50.610
So placating the carp has become a necessity

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:55.679
This explains our slug harvest discussion in the last episode and

00:05:56.050 --> 00:06:01.919
All of those slugs likely end up here in the hands of the Great Carp attendant

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:08.020
Daughter of the Carp Attendant: My father is now a noble and the moment he became one

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:14.760
Daughter of the Carp Attendant: he found himself entranced by a carp, the Great Carp

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:21.240
Daughter of the Carp Attendant: For a long, long time since, he's done nothing but feed that cursed carp

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:29.600
Daughter of the Carp Attendant: Young man, please, release my father from the carps bewitching powers.

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:35.640
Daughter of the Carp Attendant: I know my father wouldn't wish for an eternity like that

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:40.100
So their father became a Noble in the lifetime of these two daughters

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:46.470
So it follows that these women might have been some of the last to come through here from Mibu village

00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:52.710
They're the only remaining humans we find in this place and they're so old now that they've basically

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:55.710
Become all but invisible to the palace Nobles

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:59.620
Because they no longer have any youth to drain

00:06:59.740 --> 00:07:08.580
Daughter of the Carp Attendant: Young man, please be careful, the palace Nobles have a craving for the vitality of youth

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:16.400
Daughter of the Carp Attendant: They can't help themselves, they want nothing but to sap away more and more of it

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:20.320
For generations wedding processions were led from Mibu village

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:28.560
Leading to the divine realm which was an honor that was bestowed only upon those who could master the Mibu technique of breathing underwater

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:33.740
And when they arrived the wedding procession was allegedly given water of the palace

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:41.449
Which can then turn you into a Noble and then you would be fit to become a citizen of the palace or were you?

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:47.389
Because behind locked doors in a dark room that leads up to the Fountainhead peak

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:51.020
There are these red Nobles of the palace

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:58.000
Whose outfits likely denote their higher rank and here they feast upon the corpses of the Okami

00:07:58.280 --> 00:08:04.760
And they do so while right behind them lie a set of white wedding palanquins

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:11.600
Palanquins that surely belonged to the wedding processions derived from Mibu village

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:15.560
And if they had no problem devouring their own kind then they certainly

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:20.539
Wouldn't have a problem draining the life force of those coming from Mibu village

00:08:20.879 --> 00:08:25.459
And if they had no problem killing them then the very least of their concerns

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:33.700
Would be the Great Carp attendant who they tricked into performing a really undignified task

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:41.860
Daughter of the Carp Attendant: You...you beasts, you tricked him all this time

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:48.660
Daughter of the Carp Attendant: Nobility this and eternity that, pretty lies to fool him

00:08:48.740 --> 00:08:55.180
Daughter of the Carp Attendant: Give him back! Father... My Father!

00:08:55.340 --> 00:09:00.940
Daughter of the Carp Attendant: Give him back!! *crying*

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:05.480
So as Fountainhead culture descended down a really dark path

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:09.919
It's no surprise that Tomoe and Takeru saw fit to leave

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:14.269
So these two are basically mirror images of Sekiro and Kuro

00:09:14.699 --> 00:09:18.529
The Divine child and their guardian just like us

00:09:19.110 --> 00:09:21.229
Except that Tomoe and Takeru

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:27.260
Descended from the Fountainhead and then began to mingle with the Ashina elites

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:31.800
Emma: Back then, Lord Genichiro and I would come here a lot

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:38.160
Emma: Lord Takeru would play the flute and Lady Tomoe would dance under the Everblossom

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:40.460
Emma: It was a wonderful sight

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:44.580
Notes that just as Takeru played the flute of the palace Nobles

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:50.260
So too did Tomoe dance like the Okami of the Fountainhead, it's a cool little detail

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:55.360
Emma: That day beneath the branches of the Everblossom tree Lady Tomoe

00:09:56.270 --> 00:09:58.270
Emma: tried to commit suicide

00:09:58.280 --> 00:09:59.390
Sekiro: Why?

00:09:59.390 --> 00:10:04.420
Emma: She said those made immortal by the oath of the Dragon's Heritage

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:06.920
Emma: Shackle their masters.

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:13.780
Sekiro: So in order for the purification to occur, the oath bound of the Dragon's Heritage must die?

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.000
Emma: Yes, precisely

00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:20.890
Speaking of the oath bound, one trait of those touched by the Divine Dragon

00:10:21.380 --> 00:10:25.090
Appears to be this streak of white atop one's scalp

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:28.780
Sekiro has it, Kuro has it, Kuro 2.0 has it

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:32.240
Hell even the Okami warrior women have it

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:38.020
But none have it more than the purple garbed lightning-bearer atop the great sakura tree

00:10:38.390 --> 00:10:40.390
Her hair is pure white

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:46.660
Perhaps a testament to the age of these eternal beings that were blessed by the Divine Dragon

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:53.760
And it bears mentioning that the actual name of the Divine Dragon in Japanese is the Sakura Dragon

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:59.319
Which is a name that suits it way better when you consider the nature of the sakura tree

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:05.499
These cherry blossoms, if you didn't know, they only bloom for one week in an entire year

00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:08.520
It's this period of exquisite beauty that

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:12.560
Sadly cannot last but is all the more beautiful for it

00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:18.260
To the Japanese, this symbolizes an acceptance of destiny, karma, and mortality

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:24.660
And this balance is really usurped and turned kind of unnatural in Sekiro

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:30.740
Because the sakura here bloom permanently and this is of course thanks to the Sakura Dragon

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:35.120
Who drifted here from the west and he probably was lost

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:43.100
Until he discovered Japan which luckily also had sakura trees and he decided to settle in this fertile land which

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:48.860
Which forced the lesser gods out and I've spoken of these lesser gods before

00:11:49.130 --> 00:11:57.010
Since it's possible that the lesser gods are the Serpent God and Buddha who were once a part of this region

00:11:57.380 --> 00:12:01.920
But I should really also be mentioning the white dragons of the tree

00:12:02.060 --> 00:12:06.340
These wise and little dudes that also fit the description

00:12:06.340 --> 00:12:09.540
Their faces can be found on the architecture of the palace

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:14.520
Thus I think it's likely that they were actually here before the dragon took root

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:21.780
They are of the tree, after all, and I reckon these little gods were merged with the

00:12:21.860 --> 00:12:27.320
divinity of the Sakura Dragon when he made their tree his own

00:12:27.460 --> 00:12:34.780
And we mentioned the white hair of the oath bound as well, something that is also seen with the old dragons

00:12:34.820 --> 00:12:38.560
They have become this really sickly white

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:43.500
Literally to because they are very sick, in contrast to the black dragons

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:51.020
these white dragons are a representation of Dragonrot and the stagnation that's afflicting us all and

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:56.100
It's actually the act of killing these white dragons that purges the affliction from the tree

00:12:56.200 --> 00:13:01.900
Which causes it to blossom, which causes the Sakura Dragon to rouse itself back to life

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:06.640
And the first thing we notice with the dragon is that it's terribly wounded

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:09.400
And there are some interesting theories on this as well

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:15.180
So first, it could be wounded because it's showing the effects of Dragonrot or

00:13:15.300 --> 00:13:17.760
Maybe it had these wounds before

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:22.080
When it was cut free from the West and drifted to Japan or

00:13:22.100 --> 00:13:23.400
An even better theory

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:31.820
It's possible that these wounds the dragon has mirror the wounds that we, Sekiro and Kuro also have sustained

00:13:31.820 --> 00:13:37.320
We are of the dragon's blood after all and just like the dragon has lost its left arm

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:41.920
We have as well, and just like the dragon has a gash on its chest

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:47.920
Kuro also cut himself with the Mortal Blade when he drew blood for the Fountainhead fragrance

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:50.740
Another really likely theory is that

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:57.800
Maybe it sustained these wounds during an earlier fight and the best candidate for a fight against the Divine Dragon

00:13:57.900 --> 00:14:02.900
Is Tomoe, who would have fought the dragon for its dragon's tears

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:10.560
And Tomoe may have also been the original owner of the second Mortal Blade, the Black Blade

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:16.140
It's easy to complete Sekiro without really realizing that the Black Blade exists

00:14:16.150 --> 00:14:20.919
But it is a supremely important item for explaining the story

00:14:21.140 --> 00:14:26.169
It's real name is "Open Gate", a weapon with the power to open a gate to the underworld

00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:31.419
Which, if you didn't know, is what happens at the end of the game when Genichiro

00:14:31.600 --> 00:14:38.420
Summons his grandfather back in his prime to defeat you and it's description has one final line

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:43.980
One that reads, "I beseech you make offerings for the dragon's blood"

00:14:44.240 --> 00:14:47.460
This links the weapon to the Divine Dragon and

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:53.020
While it's the most sinister example of the Divine Dragon wanting an offering

00:14:53.140 --> 00:15:01.220
It's not the only example of offerings, the Okami dance as an offering, the Mibu were brought here as marital offerings

00:15:01.280 --> 00:15:08.100
Those of the Fountainhead had a practice of cutting spirit emblems from their flesh with a ceremonial knife

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:13.260
and there's also a shrine maiden here who has passed away praying at the dragon's shrine

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:18.720
And then there's the Black Blade which was allegedly used for offerings as well.

00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:23.300
And now let me explain why the Black Blade would have belonged to Tomoe

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:31.100
First we know that Tomoe wanted to sever immortality and for this she needed the tears of the Divine Dragon

00:15:31.620 --> 00:15:36.940
However, while the Black Blade could wound the Divine Dragon it couldn't impart its tears

00:15:36.940 --> 00:15:44.520
And for this she would need the red Mortal Blade, which is actually named "The Gracious Gift of Tears"

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:52.420
It's designed for this purpose. But, unfortunately for her, it was hidden away by the Senpou High Priest and

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:54.480
No matter what Tomoe tried

00:15:54.500 --> 00:16:02.680
She could not get him to reveal its whereabouts and she did try to get it which puts her at odds with the Divine Dragon

00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:09.700
Second, those Tomoe was closest to in Ashina ended up knowing a lot about the Black Blade

00:16:09.980 --> 00:16:13.760
A scroll describing it is left outside of Isshin's quarters

00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:19.500
Genichiro trained under Tomoe and later managed to find the Black Blade

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:24.600
And Takeru wrote of beheading with the Mortal Blade an act that Genichiro

00:16:24.760 --> 00:16:27.840
Performs with the Black Blade at the end of the game

00:16:27.860 --> 00:16:29.480
My point here, is that Tomoe

00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:36.340
Influenced the lives of so many people and it's crazy to imagine that we might not learn more about her in the future

